# Noggle the Mind replaces only creature types (CR 205.3d, the reminder "It loses ... all other creature types"): Bot2's Dryad Arbor, a green
# Land Creature - Forest Dryad, becomes a colorless Forest Noggle - it keeps its land type Forest (a land type, not a creature type, CR 205.3i)
# and loses Dryad.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Noggle the Mind
Island x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Dryad Arbor
Island x19

[Actions]
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Dryad Arbor.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
? Bot2.Battlefield.Dryad Arbor.Subtypes = Dryad; Forest
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Noggle the Mind.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Dryad Arbor)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Dryad Arbor.Types = Land; Creature
Bot2.Battlefield.Dryad Arbor.Subtypes = Forest; Noggle
Bot2.Battlefield.Dryad Arbor.Colors = (absent)
